---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Expo Integration" activeNav="/guides/expo-integration">
  <h1>Expo Integration</h1>
  <p>
    Connect your Expo account to manage EAS builds, submissions, and credentials
    from App Manager. The integration supports the full Expo lifecycle:
    connect, sync, import, provision, and proxy.
  </p>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <p>Expo integration must be enabled by the operator:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`INTEGRATIONS_ENABLED=true
EXPO_INTEGRATION_ENABLED=true`} />

  <h2>1. Connect your Expo account</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/acme/integrations/expo \\
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY' \\
  -H 'Accept: application/json' \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{
    "access_token": "EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN",
    "account_name": "acme"
  }'`} />

  <p>
    The access token is encrypted and stored. It is never returned in API responses.
    Reconnecting with the same Expo account replaces the token.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Sync projects</h2>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/acme/integrations/INTEGRATION_ID/expo/sync \\
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY'`} />

  <h2>3. Link a project to an app</h2>
  <p>Create a new Expo project:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="json" code={`{
  "integration_id": "019f...",
  "mode": "create",
  "sync_metadata": true
}`} />

  <p>Or link to an existing project:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="json" code={`{
  "integration_id": "019f...",
  "mode": "existing",
  "expo_project_id": "019f...",
  "sync_metadata": true
}`} />

  <h2>4. Sync identifiers</h2>
  <p>Compare and sync identifiers between App Manager and Expo:</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/acme/apps/customer-app/expo/identifiers/sync \\
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY'`} />

  <h2>5. Provision identifiers and credentials</h2>
  <p>
    Provision a remote Expo identifier with all supported credentials:
  </p>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`curl -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/acme/apps/customer-app/expo/identifiers/IDENTIFIER_ID/provision \\
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY' \\
  -H 'Accept: application/json' \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{
    "credential_ids": ["019f...", "019f..."]
  }'`} />

  <p>
    Without <code>credential_ids</code>, all supported credentials with uploaded files are sent.
    Remote credential resources are immutable — a repeated push creates a new resource.
  </p>

  <h2>Expo proxy</h2>
  <p>
    The proxy forwards requests to Expo's API. The <code>Authorization</code> header is
    replaced with the saved Expo token.
  </p>
  <p><strong>GraphQL proxy:</strong></p>
  <CodeBlock lang="bash" code={`curl -X POST \\
  http://localhost:8000/api/v1/acme/integrations/INTEGRATION_ID/expo/graphql \\
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY' \\
  -H 'Accept: application/json' \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{
    "query": "query Project($id: String!) { app { byId(appId: $id) { id name slug } } }",
    "variables": {"id": "EXPO_PROJECT_ID"},
    "operation_name": "Project"
  }'`} />

  <p>
    The <code>integrations:proxy</code> scope is a high-trust scope that can read remote Expo secrets.
    Do not issue it to runners that only need custom endpoints.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
